    "company_name": "ABC Supply",
    "raw_content": "ABC Supply also supports contractors through ABC Supply Interiors, Inc. (formerly L&W Supply) and ABC Supply Outdoor Solutions, a division of ABC Supply Co., Inc. (formerly Town & Country Industries). Headquartered in Beloit, Wisconsin, ABC Supply has more than 1,000 locations across the U.S. and Canada. More information is available at www.abcsupply.com.\n\n# # # [...] Search Proxy\n\n Monday through Friday. Michael Longo will manage the new branch.\n\nLongo initially joined ABC Supply in 2009 as an inside sales associate at the Fort Myers, Florida, location. For the last six years, he has held roles in the company\u2019s window department \u2014 which has grown significantly under his leadership.\n\n\u201cMichael is deeply rooted in our mission and values,\u201d said ABC Supply Southeast Region Vice President Frank Marcoccio. \u201cHis dedication to our associates and customers was the key to his success in past positions, and I am confident he will help contractors in the Bonita Springs market grow their businesses.\u201d [...] The branch\u2019s phone number is (239) 596-8626. Contractors can also request aerial measurement reports, place and review orders and check the status of their deliveries using myABCsupply.\n\n#### About ABC Supply\n\nABC Supply Co., Inc. is the largest wholesale distributor of roofing, select exterior and interior building products, and outdoor solutions in North America. Founded in 1982, the company focuses exclusively on serving professional contractors by providing products, services and support across major building categories.\n\nABC Supply is a 20-time Gallup Exceptional Workplace Award winner and is committed to hiring military veterans. The company also received the 2025 NAW Distributors Award, recognizing its industry leadership, community engagement and commitment to innovation.\nWikipedia\nThe Free Encyclopedia\n\n## Contents\n\n# ABC Supply\n\nABC Supply Co., Inc.\n\n|  |  |\n --- |\n|  | |\n| ABC Supply headquarters in Beloit, Wisconsin | |\n| Type | Private |\n| Industry | Roof and building materials |\n| Founded | 1982; 44 years ago (1982) |\n| Founder |  Ken Hendricks  Diane Hendricks |\n| Headquarters | Beloit, Wisconsin , U.S. |\n| Number of locations | 970 stores  |\n| Area served | United States |\n| Key people |  Diane Hendricks (chair)  Keith Rozolis (president and CEO)  Todd Buehl (CFO) |\n| Products | Building materials and tools |\n| Revenue | US$20,400,000,000 (2023)  |\n| Number of employees | 20,000 |\n| Subsidiaries | Bradco Supply |\n| Website | www.abcsupply.com | [...] ABC Supply Co., Inc. is a major, private American roofing supply company based in Beloit, Wisconsin. It also sells windows, gutters, and siding \"Siding (construction)\") for residential and commercial buildings and is the largest roofing and vinyl siding wholesale distributor \"Distribution (business)\") in the United States.\n\n## History\n\nThe company was founded in 1982 by Ken Hendricks and Diane Hendricks. It grew from a single store in Wisconsin to having over 700 branches in 49 states nationwide and sales of over 11 billion dollars.\n\nABC Supply has expanded from its original business. In early 2010, the company acquired Bradco Supply, its largest acquisition to date. [...] Annual sales topped $5.9 billion in 2015, placing it 63rd on Forbes list of largest private companies in the United States.\n\nFollowing the accidental death \"Falling (accident)\") of Ken Hendricks on December 21, 2007, company president David Luck was named CEO. Luck retired on December 31, 2013, and was replaced by Keith Rozolis.\n\nIn May 2020, one of the company's property locations was among those damaged by arson during the George Floyd protests in Minneapolis\u2013Saint Paul.\n\n## Awards and honors\n\nThe company has won the Gallup Great Workplace Award for eleven consecutive years, from 2007 to 2017.[failed verification]\n\n## Corporate sponsorship\n\nIt sponsored A. J. Foyt Enterprises' #14 and #4 IndyCar Series cars.\nWikipedia\nThe Free Encyclopedia\n\n## Contents\n\n# ABC Supply\n\nABC Supply Co., Inc.\n\n|  |  |\n --- |\n|  | |\n| ABC Supply headquarters in Beloit, Wisconsin | |\n| Type | Private |\n| Industry | Roof and building materials |\n| Founded | 1982; 44 years ago (1982) |\n| Founder |  Ken Hendricks  Diane Hendricks |\n| Headquarters | Beloit, Wisconsin , U.S. |\n| Number of locations | 970 stores  |\n| Area served | United States |\n| Key people |  Diane Hendricks (chair)  Keith Rozolis (president and CEO)  Todd Buehl (CFO) |\n| Products | Building materials and tools |\n| Revenue | US$20,400,000,000 (2023)  |\n| Number of employees | 20,000 |\n| Subsidiaries | Bradco Supply |\n| Website | www.abcsupply.com | [...] ABC Supply Co., Inc. is a major, private American roofing supply company based in Beloit, Wisconsin. It also sells windows, gutters, and siding \"Siding (construction)\") for residential and commercial buildings and is the largest roofing and vinyl siding wholesale distributor \"Distribution (business)\") in the United States.\n\n## History\n\nThe company was founded in 1982 by Ken Hendricks and Diane Hendricks. It grew from a single store in Wisconsin to having over 700 branches in 49 states nationwide and sales of over 11 billion dollars.\n\nABC Supply has expanded from its original business. In early 2010, the company acquired Bradco Supply, its largest acquisition to date.\n# Corporate Officers\n\n## Diane M. Hendricks\n\n### Founder\n\nDiane Hendricks\n\nDiane M. Hendricks co-founded building products distributor ABC Supply Co., Inc. with her late husband Kenneth Hendricks in 1982. Diane and Ken also founded Hendricks Holding Co., Inc. which presides over a diverse portfolio of businesses including manufacturing, distribution, real estate development, construction, recycling and life sciences.\n\nABC is the largest distributor of roofing materials in North America and a leading distributor of siding, windows, gutter, wallboard, metal framing and ceiling tiles. ABC has earned 18 Gallup Exceptional Workplace Awards and two Glassdoor Employees\u2019 Choice Awards for Best Places to Work for its commitment to creating an employee-first, engaging culture.\n# Leadership\n\nDiane Hendricks\n\n### Diane M. Hendricks\n\n#### Founder\n\nDiane M. Hendricks co-founded building products distributor ABC Supply Co., Inc. with her late husband Kenneth Hendricks in 1982. Diane and Ken also founded Hendricks Holding Co., Inc. which presides over a diverse portfolio of businesses including manufacturing, distribution, real estate development, construction, recycling and life sciences.\n\n### Keith Rozolis\n\n#### Chief Executive Officer\n\nKeith Rozolis leads ABC Supply\u2019s branch and manufacturing operations, its divisional companies and its marketing and merchandising groups and focuses on the continued development of strategic initiatives that will position ABC Supply for ongoing success.\n\n### Mike Jost\n\n#### President and Chief Operating Officer [...] ### Mike Jost\n\n#### President and Chief Operating Officer\n\nAs president and COO, Mike Jost leads the performance and operations of the company's locations across North America. He also oversees ABC's branch and manufacturing operations, as well as its divisional companies, including ABC Supply Interiors. Jost's leadership extends to key areas such as marketing, merchandising, real estate, education, fleet, safety, and national business development, driving success across the organization.\n\n### Jim Anderson\n\n#### Chief Financial Officer\n\nJim Anderson oversees a variety of functions that are vital to the company\u2019s continued growth, including corporate development, accounting and financial reporting, financial planning and analysis, treasury, tax, internal audit, risk management and credit. [...] #### President of ABC Supply\u2019s Branch Operations\n\nAs President of ABC Supply\u2019s Branch Operations, Jonathan Shepard leads all branch field teams and oversees operations at the company\u2019s National Support Center, ensuring efficiency and enhanced customer service.\n\n### Tony Vaden\n\n#### Chief Information Officer\n\nAs Chief Information Officer, Tony Vaden oversees all aspects of ABC Supply\u2019s information technology systems in North America.\n\n### Matt Belcher\n\n#### Southwest Region Vice President\n\nAs vice president of ABC Supply\u2019s Southwest Region, Matt Belcher is responsible for overseeing business performance and growth across the seven-state region.\n\n### Matt Cooper\n\n#### West Region Vice President\n### Mike Jost\n\nPresident and Chief Operating Officer\n\nAs president and COO, Mike Jost leads the performance and operations of the company's locations across North America. He also oversees ABC's branch and manufacturing operations, as well as its divisional companies, including ABC Supply Interiors. Jost's leadership extends to key areas such as marketing, merchandising, real estate, education, fleet, safety, and national business development, driving success across the organization.\n\nImage 7\n\n### Jim Anderson\n\nChief Financial Officer\n\nJim Anderson oversees a variety of functions that are vital to the company\u2019s continued growth, including corporate development, accounting and financial reporting, financial planning and analysis, treasury, tax, internal audit, risk management and credit. [...] ## Delivering On The American Dream Since 1982\n\nWith every decision they make, our leadership stays true to the Core Values ABC Supply started from the beginning: The highest level of respect for both customers and our associates.\n\n## ABC Supply Leadership Team\n\nImage 4\n\n### Diane M. Hendricks\n\nFounder\n\nDiane M. Hendricks co-founded building products distributor ABC Supply Co., Inc. with her late husband Kenneth Hendricks in 1982. Diane and Ken also founded Hendricks Holding Co., Inc. which presides over a diverse portfolio of businesses including manufacturing, distribution, real estate development, construction, recycling and life sciences.\n\nImage 5\n\n### Keith Rozolis\n\nChief Executive Officer [...] Image 5\n\n### Keith Rozolis\n\nChief Executive Officer\n\nKeith Rozolis leads ABC Supply\u2019s branch and manufacturing operations, its divisional companies and its marketing and merchandising groups and focuses on the continued development of strategic initiatives that will position ABC Supply for ongoing success.\n\nImage 6\n\n### Mike Jost\n\nPresident and Chief Operating Officer\nABC Truck in front of a barn painted with an American flag\n\n# About Us\n\n## Built On A Foundation Of Respect\n\nSince 1982, we have become North America\u2019s largest wholesale distributor of roofing supplies. Plus, one of the largest distributors of siding, windows and other select exterior and interior building products, tools and related supplies.\n\nLearn more about our journey and what drives us to serve our contractor customers day in and day out. You\u2019ve come to the right place.\n\n## About Us Sections\n\n### Leadership\n\n### Mission & Vision\n\n### Core Purpose and Values\n\n### Our History\n\n### In The Community\n\n### Careers\n\n### Ken Hendricks Award\n\n### Acquisitions\n\n\u00a9 2026 ABC Supply Co. Inc.\nABC Supply Co., Inc. is a major, private American roofing supply company based in Beloit, Wisconsin. It also sells windows, gutters, and siding \"Siding (construction)\") for residential and commercial buildings and is the largest roofing and vinyl siding wholesale distributor \"Distribution (business)\") in the United States.\n\n## History\n\nThe company was founded in 1982 by Ken Hendricks and Diane Hendricks. It grew from a single store in Wisconsin to having over 700 branches in 49 states nationwide and sales of over 11 billion dollars.\n\nABC Supply has expanded from its original business. In early 2010, the company acquired Bradco Supply, its largest acquisition to date. [...] Wikipedia\nThe Free Encyclopedia\n\n## Contents\n\n# ABC Supply\n\nABC Supply Co., Inc.\n\n|  |  |\n --- |\n|  | |\n| ABC Supply headquarters in Beloit, Wisconsin | |\n| Type | Private |\n| Industry | Roof and building materials |\n| Founded | 1982; 44 years ago (1982) |\n| Founder |  Ken Hendricks  Diane Hendricks |\n| Headquarters | Beloit, Wisconsin , U.S. |\n| Number of locations | 970 stores  |\n| Area served | United States |\n| Key people |  Diane Hendricks (chair)  Keith Rozolis (president and CEO)  Todd Buehl (CFO) |\n| Products | Building materials and tools |\n| Revenue | US$20,400,000,000 (2023)  |\n| Number of employees | 20,000 |\n| Subsidiaries | Bradco Supply |\n| Website | www.abcsupply.com |",
