    "raw_content": "Skip to content\n\nSubscribe to our newsletter\n\n Flooring News\n\n# Abbey Carpet Seventh Largest Private Firm In Flori\n\nBonita, Springs, FL, Oct. 1\u2013Mixed in among a list of Florida\u2019s top private companies is a sole mention of Bonita Springs, according to the Bonita Banner.\n\nIt belongs to Abbey Carpet. Though born in Sacramento, CA, the national carpet franchise grew to post $1.8 billion in sales through roughly 1,200 franchise stores nationwide while operating its headquarters from a two-story building tucked in a corner of the Bonita Bay Executive Center. The revenue made it the seventh largest privately held company in the state, as measured by Florida Trend magazine. Abbey Carpet doesn\u2019t own any of the stores bearing its name.\nwas merged into Abbey Carpet Co. of Florida, Inc. which subsequently changed its name to Abbey Carpet Co.,Inc. ABBEY is now a corporation organized and existing under the laws of the State of Florida with its principal offices located at 3471 Bonita Bay Boulevard, Bonita Springs, Florida 34134. [...] # Abbey Carpet & Floor\n\nAbbey Carpet Co., Inc.\n\nSave\n\n#### Company Information\n\n3471 Bonita Bay Boulevard, Bonita Springs, Florida 34134\n\nwww.abbevcarnet.com\n\n(/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection) [...] Abbey Carpet Co., Inc. was incorporated in 1958 under the laws of the State of California as a retail carpeting store. Abbey Carpet Co., Inc. started as a family owned business and by 1966 had grown from one store to eleven stores. In 1966, Abbey Carpet Co., Inc discontinued operating any retail businesses and operated only as a buying service centered in Sacramento, California. Abbey Carpet Co., Inc. has continued to offer such buying service memberships and in 1971 became one of the first franchises to be registered under California\u2019s Franchise Investment Law. On November 20, 1995, Abbey Carpet Co. of Florida, Inc. was incorporated under the laws of the State of Florida. Effective January 1, 1996, Abbey Carpet Co., Inc. was merged into Abbey Carpet Co. of Florida, Inc. which\n### Abbey Carpet and Flooring\n\n## About Company\n\nAbbey Carpets is a carpet and flooring business that got its start 26 years ago with a dream that soon became a vision. After working for a number of years in the carpeting and flooring industry, Mr. Abdul Rehman, the founder of the establishment, dreamt of providing people with quality flooring. He had a vision to serve customers with only the best that customer service has to offer. Abbey Carpets received a worthy addition to the team when 8 years ago Mr. Ayub Choudhry joined the team. With a combined industry experience of 40 years in the field, Mr. Rehman and Mr. Choudhry take pride in serving you!\n\nFrom its inception, Abbey Carpets Inc. was established on four pillars that continue to be honored today.\n\n### 1. Quality of product\n# Dennis Kemerer\nOwner and CEO Abbey Carpet & Floor\nAdrian, Michigan, United States, US  \n150 connections, 163 followers\n\n## About\nVice President of BNI Lenawee 8 year member<br><br>\n\n## Experience\n### Owner and President  \nAbbey Carpet & Floor  \nDec 2005 - Present   \nUnited States  \nRetail Flooring and interior finishes and installation\n\n### Operations Manager  \nAbbey Carpet and floor  \nNov 2005 - Present   \nN/A  \n\n### General Manager  \nCircuit City  \nFeb 2003 - Nov 2005   \nN/A  \n\n### Regional Director  \nHollywood Entertainment  \nJan 1990 - Jan 2002   \nkansas, missouri, arkansas, oklahoma, iowa  \nResponsible for operations of 70 + locations in five states.\n\n## Education\n### Delta College  \nN/A  \n1983 - 1984  \nNone\n\n## Publications\nN/A\n\n## Honors & Awards\nN/A\n\n## Certifications\nN/A [...] - Allison Ott  \nNone  \nView Post  \n\n## People Also Viewed\n- Heather Fountain (Bronxton) - \n- Gregg Holt (City Restore Inc) - \n- Dave Casey (Amazon) - \n- Danielle Veith (TMart Operations I, LLC dba Dunkin'/Baskin Robbins) - \n- Frank Ferreira (ECMKing.com) - \n- 