u2019s strategic growth through trust-based selling.\n\nIn addition to his leadership background, Dominie is a sought-after industry speaker and trusted consultant. He served as a Mohawk University trainer for 13 years, creating programs that taught dealers how to sell through service and relationship-building. [...] In his new role, Dominie will work closely with the franchise development team to grow Abbey Carpet & Floor and Floors To Go membership nationwide while strengthening relationships with existing members.\n\n Tags\n Abbey Carpet\n executive appointments\n Paul Dominie\n\nPrevious article\n\nRetailers React: What is the biggest customer concern right now?\n\nNext article\n\nNAFCD + NBMDA Annual Convention gives back to the industry\n\n#### RELATED ARTICLES\n\nInstallation\n\n### Platform Performance assembles leadership team\n\nFeatured Post\n\n### Mohawk announces CEO succession plan\n\nCarpet\n\n### Kate Judd joins Tai Ping, Edward Fields\n\n#### Must Read\n\nNews\n\n### Schattdecor realigns executive board responsibilities\n\nFCNews Staff -  0\nA cornerstone of Abbey\u2019s culture, she noted, is its emphasis on mentorship and knowledge sharing between seasoned employees and newer team members. The company intentionally pairs incoming talent with long-standing employees to foster collaboration and continuity.\n\n\u201cThis way, you\u2019re not reinventing the wheel,\u201d Butler explained. \u201cYou\u2019re leveraging the best of both worlds\u2014fresh ideas and new energy from younger employees combined with the deep relationships and institutional knowledge of long-time team members.\u201d [...] #### Building the next generation\n\nThe company\u2019s generational transition is best illustrated by the involvement of chairman, president and CEO Phil Gutierrez\u2019s granddaughters in the business. Kailie Gutierrez recently joined Abbey\u2019s marketing department after graduating from Ole Miss with a degree in marketing. Her younger sister, Ali, has also gained experience working at the company\u2019s corporate retail store in Naples while attending college.\n\n\u201cThere\u2019s definitely pressure because I know how hard my grandfather has worked for this business,\u201d Kailie Gutierrez said. \u201cI\u2019m never going to fill his shoes, but I would like to grow into my own role within the company.\u201d [...] News\n Category\n  + Carpet\n  + Resilient\n  + Wood\n  + Laminate\n  + Tile\n  + Technology\n  + Installation\n  + Underlayment\n Columns\n  + Al\u2019s Column\n  + Editorials\n  + Financial\n  + Guest Column\n  + Installments\n  + Lessons Learned\n  + Lisbiz Strategies\n  + Marketing Mastery\n  + Retailer2retailer\n Videos\n Classifieds\n Archives\n Advertise\n Subscribe\n Sign Up For Our Newsletters\n\nLogo\n\nSign Up For Our Newsletters\n\nLogo\n\n Advertise\n\nMore\n\n# Abbey Carpet embraces next-gen leadership\n\nBy Steve Feldman\n\nHomeFeatured CompanyAbbey Carpet embraces next-gen leadership\n\nAbbey Carpet\n\nAbbey leadership is trending younger in order to support the needs of its member base.\nAt Abbey Carpets Inc., our vision is to provide customers with a friendly and memorable experience in which we provide excellent customer service, install the highest quality flooring, at the lowest prices, and at the customer\u2019s earliest convenience. We believe flooring is instrumental in enhancing lifestyles.\n\n### Fast Pickup/Delivery\n\n### Quick installation\n\n### Prompt after sale service\n\n## Contact Us\n\n### Abbey Carpets Inc. 966 Dundas Street East Mississauga, Ont. L4Y 4H5\n\n### abbeycarpets@hotmail.com\n\n### Hours\n\nMon-Fri 9 am - 8 pm  \n Sat 10 am - 6 pm  \n Sun 12pm - 5 pm\n\n## Customer care\n\nHome  \nAbout Us  \nContact Us  \nRETURNS POLICY  \nPRIVACY POLICY\n\n## Product Links\n\nAREA RUGS  \nCARPET  \nHARDWOOD  \nLAMINATE  \nTILE / STONE  \nVINYL\n\n## Subscribe Now [...] ### Abbey Carpet and Flooring\n\n## About Company\n\nAbbey Carpets is a carpet and flooring business tha