    "raw_content": "PROFILE\n\nupgrade profile\n\nUpgrade To Receive Expanded Profile Features\n\n# Acosta Sales and Marketing Company\n\nJacksonville, Florida\n\nForbes does not accept payment for placement on lists.\n\nFrom the Editor\n\n## Last Updated Aug 20, 2024, 7:00pm EDT\n\nAcosta is a full-service sales and marketing agency, providing outsourced sales, merchandising, marketing and promotional services to manufacturers in the consumer packaged goods (CPG) industry. Headquartered in Jacksonville, Fla., Acosta has operations throughout the U.S. and Canada.\n\n## Acosta Sales and Marketing Company Stats As of August 2024\n\nIndustry\n:   Business Services & Supplies\n\nFounded\n:   1927\n\nHeadquarters\n:   Jacksonville, Florida\n\nCountry/Territory\n:   United States\n\nCEO and President\n:   Darian Pickett\n\nEmployees\n:   20,000\n### Product Connections Careers\n\n    Product Connections creates impactful brand experiences through digital and in-person events, including product sampling, shopper marketing, and more.\n\n    View Openings\n\n    Get to Know Product Connections\n\nItem 1 of 8\n\n## Who We Are\n\nAcosta Group is headquartered in Jacksonville, Florida, but we have thousands of employees and a variety of teams generating sales for our clients all over North America and Europe.\n\nSEARCH U.S. ROLES\n\nSEARCH CANADA ROLES\n\nSEARCH GREAT BRITAIN ROLES\n\n\u201cAcosta Group is a vibrant, growing entity, and growth creates career opportunities. Our associates can explore and build careers they didn't even think were possible.\u201d\n\nBrian Wynne, President and CEO\n\nAbout Us\n\n### Build Your Career Here\nGaryAcosta.com\n\n# Gary Acosta Media\n\n#### Successful entrepreneur, investor and founder of today\u2019s leading Hispanic business organization\n\nGary Acosta is an entrepreneur, investor, and advocate for the Latino business community. He is the Co-Founder and CEO of the National Association of Hispanic Real Estate Professionals (NAHREP), the largest Latino business organization in the nation with more than 58,000 members and 100 local chapters. He is also the Co-Founder of AVANCE Global, an event platform created with media entrepreneur and New York Times bestselling author, Nely Gal\u00e1n. [...] ## PODCAST: Govies, Plutes, & Gangsters\n\nMoney. Power. Future. Latinos continue to drive the U.S. Economy with their dollar and fulfill the workforce with their skills but reap little in reward. This podcast dives into how govies (government officials), plutes (venture capitalists), and gangsters (industry trailblazers), all have a unique yet critical role to play in closing the wealth gap. Join entrepreneur and investor Gary Acosta, Co-Founder & CEO of NAHREP, the country\u2019s leading Hispanic business organization, and of L\u2019ATTITUDE, the preeminent platform for Latino economic empowerment, with powerhouse guests as they take on closing the wealth gap in the Latino community. Available in audio and video formats.\n\n### Emilio Estefan [...] Gary also founded AVANCE Sports, a non-profit dedicated to expanding Latino leadership and influence in the sports industry. He is a founding partner of L\u2019ATTITUDE Ventures, the largest venture capital fund that invests exclusively in Latino-led startups. He is the creator of the Hispanic Wealth Project, a non-profit with a mission to advance economic mobility and generational wealth in the Latino community. His video series, \u201cThe Latino Brand,\u201d shares his take on business, leadership, and the image of Latinos in America.\n\nGary attended the University of California in San Diego and Pomona College, where he played varsity basketball for Hall of Fame coach, Gregg Popovich. He lives with his family in San Diego.\n\n##### Sign up for Gary's Weekly Blog\n\n##### Never Miss an Episode\nNAHREP\nNAHREP\n\nFacebook\nfb-share-icon\nTwitter\nTweet\nLinkedIn\nShare\nInstagram\n\n### Gary Acosta\n\nCo-Founder & CEO\n\nGary Acosta is an entrepreneur, investor, and advocate for the Latino business community. He is the Co-Founder and CEO of the National Association of Hispanic Real Estate Professionals (NAHREP), the largest Latino business organization in the nation with more than 58,000 members and 100 local chapters. Under his leadership, NAHREP created the Hispanic Wealth Project, a non-profit committed to increasing household wealth in the Latino community. [...] He is a founding partner of L\u2019ATTITUDE Ventures, the largest venture capital fund in the country that invests exclusively in Latino-led startups. Over the course of his career, Gary has launched and led several companies in real estate, mortgage, and technology, including New Vista Asset Management, CounselorMax, and RealEstateEspanol.com. He also co-founded The Mortgage Collaborative, a for-profit network of more than 200 mortgage companies.\n\nGary served on the consumer advisory board of the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau (CFPB) and on advisory boards for several Fortune 500 companies, including Fannie Mae, Freddie Mac, and JP Morgan Chase. He currently serves on the boards of NAHREP and BaseCap Analytics.\n## Share this article\n\nShare this article\n\nJACKSONVILLE, Fla., Sept. 16, 2024 /PRNewswire/ -- Acosta Group has announced key leadership appointments aimed at strengthening CPG client and retail customer relationships and driving growth. Mark Rahiya joins as Group President, Omnichannel Sales and Services, and Darian Pickett has been named Chief Global Client Officer. Ashley Roehm has been promoted to President of Acosta Sales Agency, while Jami McDermid will continue as President of CROSSMARK. Lisa Koth will now serve as Acosta Group Chief Strategy Officer and EVP, Acosta Europe, expanding her role to include leadership of Acosta Europe. [...] DARIAN PICKETT NAMED CHIEF GLOBAL CLIENT OFFICER\n\nDarian Pickett, a seasoned industry veteran and accomplished Acosta Group leader, has been appointed Chief Global Client Officer, representing a significant investment in the organization's clients. Since joining Acosta in 1991, Pickett has held leadership roles across every aspect of the company's operations. He is known for navigating market changes successfully while building and maintaining strong client relationships. [...] Lisa Koth will now serve as Acosta Group Chief Strategy Officer and EVP, Acosta Europe, expanding her role to include leadership of Acosta Europe following the company's acquisition of the Dee Set Group in the UK. Koth joined the company as a Senior Strategy Director in 2021 and was promoted to SVP, Acosta Group Chief Strategy Officer in 2022. She has led several critical acquisitions over the past two years, including the organization's recent acquisition of CROSSMARK and Product Connections.\nAcosta\nAcosta Group Logo\n\n# Inside Acosta Group\u2019s Leadership Development Program\n\nFacebook\n\nAre you ready to kickstart your career and take your leadership potential to the next level? Acosta Group is committed to empowering future leaders with the tools, experiences, and connections necessary to make a meaningful impact.\n\nOur Leadership Development Program (LDP) is a transformational 18-month rotational journey for early-career professionals eager to grow, learn, and lead.\n\nImagine rotating through several dynamic areas of our business, including Retail, Foodservice, Business Intelligence, Sales, and Marketing.\n\nEach rotation immerses you in: [...] In the nearly 20 years since the LDP program began, we\u2019ve seen alumni accelerate across all areas of the business. Learn more about LDP alumni\u2019s career trajectories here.\n\n### Ready to Lead? Your Journey Starts Here\n\nIf you\u2019re an ambitious and curious early-career professional ready to build real-world experience and connect with inspiring mentors, the Acosta Group Leadership Development Program is your launchpad to success. In just 18 months, you\u2019ll rotate through key areas of our business, hone your skills, and uncover where your unique talents can make the biggest impact.\n\nTake the first step toward unlocking your potential. Join our LDP talent pool today and get ready to shape your future here.\n\nFacebook\n\nperson being handed google store shopping bag [...] ### Harrison\n\n\u201cIt has been an incredible journey! The opportunities to collaborate with different parts of the company have been endless. Being exposed to a variety of roles, functions, company cultures and making lasting connections at all levels has been the most rewarding part. Acosta Group is a people business!\u201d\n\n### Benjamin\n\n\u201cOne of the highlights for me was the opportunity to travel to Nashville to support the Amazon Ops Live event. This was a valuable experience, allowing me to see everything that goes into running a successful event and how every team had to work together to drive results.\u201d\n\n### Daniel\nLogo Logo Logo Logo Logo\n\n## The people, the power and the knowledge to achieve your goals.\n\nAcosta is a global sales and marketing expert with over 30,000 employees working with hundreds of the world\u2019s leading brands. 90 years of heritage mean that we have seen a thing or two and we have access to data and insight that spans every channel. [...] ### Strength in diversity\n\nRich in talent from different generations, backgrounds, genders and life experiences. Our diversity allows us to develop and deliver innovative solutions to your problems. Our work environment has it\u2019s foundations in our values, meaning employees can be themselves at work and perform to the best of their abilities.\n\n### Sustainability\n\nWe conduct business with integrity, care and community at our heart- whether that be the areas we work or respect for our planet. We aim to promote cultures at Acosta that minimise our impact on the planet and endeavour to uphold our responsibility to respect our local communities.\n\n### Acosta Cares [...] ### Acosta Cares\n\nBeing a good company means much more than achieving a healthy bottom line. At Acosta, giving back is encouraged and we support our team to benefit the community. Acosta Cares is our Corporate Social Responsibility programme and we are proud to support local grass root charities, organise events and fundraising efforts through this.\n\nRecent examples have included running a Tough Mudder for a local hospice and sponsoring some of our industry charity\u2019s fundraisers. Whether big or small, we contribute to the communities in which we work.\n\n### Supporting our industry charity, GroceryAid.\nAbout Us\n\n### Build Your Career Here\n\nThe best companies are created through the collective talents of individuals. That's why we're obsessed with developing our people, both personally and professionally.\n\n Early Career Opportunities\n\n### Find Your Fit\n\nWhether you desire the versatility of part-time positions or the commitment of full-time roles, we're your gateway to endless opportunities.\n\nSearch Open Positions\n\n## Beware of Recruitment Scams\n\nYour safety is our priority. Acosta Group and our affiliated agencies will never ask for money during the application process. We only contact candidates using official email addresses ending in: @acosta.com, @actionlink.com, @corefoodservice.com, @crossmark.com, @deeset.co.uk, @mosaic.com, @premiumretail.com, or @productconnections.com. [...] ### Product Connections Careers\n\n    Product Connections creates impactful brand experiences through digital and in-person events, including product sampling, shopper marketing, and more.\n\n    View Openings\n\n    Get to Know Product Connections\n\nItem 1 of 8\n\n## Who We Are\n\nAcosta Group is headquartered in Jacksonville, Florida, but we have thousands of employees and a variety of teams generating sales for our clients all over North America and Europe.\n\nSEARCH U.S. ROLES\n\nSEARCH CANADA ROLES\n\nSEARCH GREAT BRITAIN ROLES\n\n\u201cAcosta Group is a vibrant, growing entity, and growth creates career opportunities. Our associates can explore and build careers they didn't even think were possible.\u201d\n\nBrian Wynne, President and CEO\n\nAbout Us\n\n### Build Your Career Here",
