    "company_name": "AgroLiquid",
    "raw_content": "#### Related Topics\n\n#### Recent in Events\n\nFarm Progress Show grounds at sunrise\nHorses and ranchers\nMichigan Farmer Logo\n\n# AgroLiquid to expand in Florida\n\nMichigan Bits: Vote near on carrot checkoff; Stabenow calls for coalition to push farm bill; and MFB Educator of the Year is chosen.\n\nMarch 26, 2024\n\n3D rendering of a new AgroLiquid facility\n\nAgroLiquid, headquartered in St. Johns, Mich., recently announced it will construct a 48,355-square-foot production facility in Lake City, Fla.\n\nThe company says the new facility, situated on nearly 20 acres within the North Florida Mega Industrial Park, will help provide liquid fertilizer closer to customers in the U.S. Southeast through faster and more efficient services. [...] Construction is underway, and the facility is expected to be fully operational by early next year.\n\nFor information about AgroLiquid's other locations and products, visit agroliquid.com.\n\n## Carrot farmers to vote on program\n\nBetween April 1 to 12, Michigan\u2019s carrot producers can vote on continuing the Carrot Industry Development Program in a referendum conducted by the Michigan Department of Agriculture and Rural Development.\n\nBallots will be mailed by MDARD to carrot producers on March 25. Producers are eligible to vote if they produced and sold carrots for human consumption, valued at more than $800, in any one of the last three years. [...] '%3e%3cpath%20fill-rule='evenodd'%20clip-rule='evenodd'%20d='M7.39998%2012.8H14.2L17.3%201.20001H7.39998C4.19998%201.20001%201.59998%203.80001%201.59998%207.00001C1.59998%2010.2%204.19998%2012.8%207.39998%2012.8Z'%20fill='white'/%3e%3cpath%20fill-rule='evenodd'%20clip-rule='evenodd'%20d='M22.6%200H7.40002C3.50002%200%200.400024%203.1%200.400024%207C0.400024%2010.9%203.50002%2014%207.40002%2014H22.6C26.5%2014%2029.6%2010.9%2029.6%207C29.6%203.1%2026.4%200%2022.6%200ZM1.60002%207C1.60002%203.8%204.20002%201.2%207.40002%201.2H17.3L14.2%2012.8H7.40002C4.20002%2012.8%201.60002%2010.2%201.60002%207Z'%20fill='%230066FF'/%3e%3cpath%20d='M24.6%203.99998C24.8%204.19998%2024.8%204.59998%2024.6%204.79998L22.5%206.99998L24.7%209.19998C24.9%209.39998%2024.9%209.79998%2024.7%209.99998C24.5%2010.2%2024\nImage 5: Michigan Farm News\n\n Eventually, AgroLiquid's 48,355-square-foot site will feature multiple tanks that can hold 4.5 million gallons of fertilizer product and 15-plus million gallons of fertilizer components. There will also be a 15-car rail siding for staging, loading and unloading. | Courtesy photo \n\n November 14, 2025 \n\n November 14, 2025 \n\n Crops \n\nSt. Johns-based AgroLiquid will now be able to deliver product to regional customers in just two days. At least, that\u2019ll be the case once the company completes construction of its new manufacturing and distribution facility in Lake City, Florida, next spring. [...] AgroLiquid is the first onsite partner/tenant of the North Florida Mega Industrial Park along U.S. Highway 90, on the edge of the Osceola National Forest. Discussions on the company\u2019s Lake City facility started in 2022, but several delays \u2014 including awaiting county and city infrastructure and permit approvals, and Hurricane Milton \u2014 pushed back site plans.\n\nHowever, the site is now zoned for 8 million square feet.\n\n\u201cWe will be able to minimize environmental impacts associated with long-distance hauling, as the Southeast region was previously serviced by our Michigan and Iowa sites,\u201d Bancroft said.\n\n\u201cThis potentially reduces transportation costs as well.\u201d\n\nThe Lake City site manager is Jeff Herald, former logistics coordinator at the company\u2019s Ashley, Michigan, facility. [...] Each year, AgroLiquid supplies thousands of customers and retailers in the United States and abroad. In January, AgroLiquid finalized the acquisition of Monty\u2019s Plant Food Co., a Louisville, Kentucky, manufacturer of plant and soil enhancement products.\n\nREAD NEXT: AGROLIQUID ACQUIRES MONTY\u2019S PLANT FOOD CO. IN \u2018PERFECT COMBINATION\u2019\n\n\u201cThe Lake City facility expands our footprint to better serve growers in the Southeast, specifically,\u201d added Bancroft, noting the facility will streamline operations and reduce transportation time to \u201cget products in the hands of growers.\u201d\nFarm News Media \n\nImage 5: Michigan Farm News\n\n \"We've come from humble beginnings, and those who supported us along the way continue to inspire us to give back in return,\u201d said AgroLiquid founder Troy Bancroft. The Bancroft family is actively involved in managing the company, including, from left to right, Jill, Troy, and sons Gerrit, Albert and Nick. | Photo by AgroLiquid \n\n August 22, 2024 \n\n August 22, 2024 \n\n From The Field \n\nThe Liquid Cares program started as a simple way for St. Johns-based AgroLiquid's founding family to help their community. Over the years, it grew quietly, and in 2022, it transformed into something much bigger; a fully funded philanthropic initiative. [...] Now, this reimagined program, deeply rooted in the Bancroft family's legacy, is making a powerful impact, supporting communities and shining a light on the agricultural industry.\n\n\"Liquid Cares was designed to support our employees and the communities they live in, where we could roll up our sleeves and help in a meaningful way,\" said Troy Bancroft, AgroLiquid founder and Chairman of the Board.\n\n\"By extending our family culture of philanthropy to the communities where our employees live, we're creating a sense of purpose that reaches beyond our business.\"\nAgroLiquid, founded by Troy Bancroft and his father-in-law, Douglas Cook, in 1983, remains a family business both in its ownership and direction. Today, the company manufactures plant nutrition products and provides service globally to crop operations, both large and small.\n\nAgroLiquid now operates five manufacturing plants located in Ashley, Mich., Williams, Iowa, Goodland, Kansas, Stockton, Calif, and Eastman, Ga. The company\u2019s sales account managers support a network of more than 120 independent retail partners and hundreds of highly-trained sales representatives.\n\nFor more than 35 years, AgroLiquid has been on a mission to engineer the best plant nutrition products while safeguarding crops, the soil, and the environment. [...] November 16, 2020 \n\n November 16, 2020 \n\n From The Field \n\nSt. Johns-based AgroLiquid\u2019s board of directors announced their selection of Nick Bancroft as the company\u2019s next CEO a role currently held by AgroLiquid founder Troy Bancroft who announced his plans to transition to a more strategic role as president of the company\u2019s board of directors and a member of the company\u2019s leadership team.\n\n\u201cNick has demonstrated exceptional leadership and management abilities as vice president for the past 10 years,\u201d Troy said. \u201cHe brings the vision and insight needed to lead AgroLiquid into the future.\u201d [...] Image 5: Michigan Farm News\n\n AgroLiquid founder and current CEO, Troy Bancroft (left) has announced his plans to transition to a more strategic role as president of the company\u2019s board of directors and a member of the company\u2019s leadership team. Nick Bancroft (right), who has served as AgroLiquid\u2019s vice president for 10 years, has been selected by the company\u2019s board of directors to take over as CEO. | Photo by AgroLiquid \n\n November 16, 2020 \n\n November 16, 2020 \n\n From The Field\nNovember 16, 2020 \n\n November 16, 2020 \n\n From The Field \n\nSt. Johns-based AgroLiquid\u2019s board of directors announced their selection of Nick Bancroft as the company\u2019s next CEO a role currently held by AgroLiquid founder Troy Bancroft who announced his plans to transition to a more strategic role as president of the company\u2019s board of directors and a member of the company\u2019s leadership team.\n\n\u201cNick has demonstrated exceptional leadership and management abilities as vice president for the past 10 years,\u201d Troy said. \u201cHe brings the vision and insight needed to lead AgroLiquid into the future.\u201d [...] \u201cI look forward to leading AgroLiquid and driving performance forward,\u201d Nick said. \u201cI am honored to work with our employees, retail partners and industry partners as we further AgroLiquid\u2019s mission to Prosper the Farmer.\u201d\n\nIn leaving the day-to-day operation of the company in Nick\u2019s capable hands, Troy looks forward to focusing on strategy and further growing AgroLiquid as a privately held business.\n\n\u201cHis insight will be valuable to both the AgroLiquid board of directors and the leadership team,\u201d Nick said. \u201cWe look forward to his continued work with AgroLiquid\u2019s valuable employees and many agricultural organizations.\u201d [...] Image 5: Michigan Farm News\n\n AgroLiquid founder and current CEO, Troy Bancroft (left) has announced his plans to transition to a more strategic role as president of the company\u2019s board of directors and a member of the company\u2019s leadership team. Nick Bancroft (right), who has served as AgroLiquid\u2019s vice president for 10 years, has been selected by the company\u2019s board of directors to take over as CEO. | Photo by AgroLiquid \n\n November 16, 2020 \n\n November 16, 2020 \n\n From The Field\nTroy Bancroft: We want to continue to be a recognized leader in innovative agriculture. For more than 35 years, we have been on a mission to engineer the best plant nutrition products while safeguarding the crop, the soil, and the environment. We try to do things that are good for our industry as a whole as opposed to good just for AgroLiquid.\n\nTroy Bancroft is the cofounder of AgroLiquid and the president of AgroLiquid\u2019s board of directors. He can be contacted at troy.bancroft@agroliquid.com. [...] Skip to content\n\n# AgroLiquid: Leaders in Innovative Agriculture\n\nThe Michigan-based company AgroLiquid provides liquid fertilizer to boost the production of a wide variety of crops. It also conducts research and shares its agronomic expertise with farmers and its more than 250 retail partners across the United States. In this interview, cofounder Troy Bancroft talks about the company\u2019s family roots and its many branches.\n\n[siteorigin\\_widget class=\u201dSiteOrigin\\_Widget\\_Headline\\_Widget\u201d][/siteorigin\\_widget]\n\nIrrigation Leader: Please tell us about how AgroLiquid was started. [...] Irrigation Leader: What should every farmer know about AgroLiquid? \n\nTroy Bancroft: We have premium products that are readily assimilated into the plant and that mix well with other products. We can provide advice to help farmers and retail partners make the best decisions in whatever they\u2019re doing. We have over 250 retail partners across North America. We have a vested interest in partnering with them to do the best job we can. \n\nIrrigation Leader: What is your vision for the future of the company?\nFollowing the acquisition, Monty\u2019s Plant Food will continue to operate under its current name as a privately owned company, with Jeff Sangalli continuing to lead the Monty\u2019s business.\n\nAbout AgroLiquid\n\nAgroLiquid, headquartered in St. Johns, Mich., manufactures and distributes high-efficiency liquid fertilizer formulated to protect nutrients from loss to the environment. AgroLiquid\u2019s products work with, instead of against, the biology of the soil, which makes them more usable by the crop. Continuous research and product improvement, coupled with an ethical business model, keep AgroLiquid focused on its mission: \u201cTo Prosper the Farmer.\u201d\n\nAbout Monty\u2019s Plant Food Company [...] \u201cThis strategic combination allows us to bring crop nutrition technologies to growers that wouldn\u02bct otherwise be available to them,\u201d said Nick Bancroft, CEO of AgroLiquid. \u201cWhile both companies share the same goals in advancing agricultural innovation, our different approaches to achieving them will create new opportunities to optimize nutrient efficiency and productivity for growers.\u201d\n\nThe acquisition unites AgroLiquid\u02bcs expertise in liquid fertilizer solutions with Monty\u02bcs specialized knowledge in soil health and humic technology. Both companies will maintain their distinct brands and continue operating independently through the 2025 growing season to ensure seamless service to their respective customers. [...] Skip to content\n\nAgroLiquid  AgroLiquid\n\nAgroLiquid Blog\n\n# Together We Grow\n\nFeatured\n\n### AgroLiquid to Acquire Monty\u2019s Plant Food Company, Expanding Innovation in Agricultural Crop Nutrition\n\nAgroLiquid, a leader in high-efficiency crop liquid fertilizer solutions, today announced the acquisition of Monty\u2019s Plant Food Company, a Louisville-based specialist in soil health and plant nutrition technology. The acquisition, effective January 1, 2025, brings together two family-founded businesses that excel in agricultural innovation and share a commitment to farmer success.\nSkip to content\n\nAgroLiquid  AgroLiquid\n\n# High Production Agriculture Meets Responsible Nutrient Management\n\n## Our Story\n\nAgroLiquid\u2019s commitment to promoting and prospering the agriculture industry spans three generations, four countries, and all fifty of the United States.\n\nFounded by father and son-in-law team, Douglas Cook and Troy Bancroft, in 1983, AgroLiquid remains a family business both in its ownership and direction to this day. Troy Bancroft\u2019s three sons, Nick (President and Chief Executive Officer), Albert (Workplace Development Lead), and Gerrit (Operations Director) are now guiding AgroLiquid with innovative business practices and product lines that will lead the company into the future. [...] ## Commitment to Integrity\n\nFrom our products and research to our operations, our company is built on five basic principles; authenticity, humble confidence, servant leadership, commitment to greatness, and passionate engagement. It\u2019s these fundamental guidelines that have helped to make AgroLiquid the most trusted authority in agricultural nutrient management today.\n\n### Authentic\n\nWe present our customers with exactly what we do, and what our products do, to help them make informed decisions.\n\n### Humbly Confident\n\nOur team works in our customers\u2019 best interests. If we don\u2019t have the solution, we\u2019ll find someone who does.\n\n### Servant Leader\n\nOur approach means making the right decisions for our customers, as well as our community and our planet.\n\n### Committed to Greatness [...] ## Our Mission: To Prosper the Farmer\n\nWe remove the guesswork involved in producing a crop by performing extensive field research across North America. This research helps us develop and manufacture the most efficient, environmentally responsible crop nutrient products and programs available. Our fertilizers are made to optimize yields, strengthen the health of plants, and bolster the nutritional value of crops, while utilizing agricultural practices which support a sustainable future for all of us.\n\n### Our Commitment\n\n Optimize the usability and productivity of crop nutrition\n Strategize the best management practices of crop nutrition for the environment\n Lead innovation through a commitment to research\n\n## Commitment to Integrity",
