    "raw_content": "### Product Connections Careers\n\n    Product Connections creates impactful brand experiences through digital and in-person events, including product sampling, shopper marketing, and more.\n\n    View Openings\n\n    Get to Know Product Connections\n\nItem 1 of 8\n\n## Who We Are\n\nAcosta Group is headquartered in Jacksonville, Florida, but we have thousands of employees and a variety of teams generating sales for our clients all over North America and Europe.\n\nSEARCH U.S. ROLES\n\nSEARCH CANADA ROLES\n\nSEARCH GREAT BRITAIN ROLES\n\n\u201cAcosta Group is a vibrant, growing entity, and growth creates career opportunities. Our associates can explore and build careers they didn't even think were possible.\u201d\n\nBrian Wynne, President and CEO\n\nAbout Us\n\n### Build Your Career Here\nAcosta\nAcosta Group Logo\nMan on cellphone\n\n# Contact\n\nComplete the form below and we will be in touch.\n\n## Here When You Need Us\n\nWith headquarters in all the major regions we serve, getting in touch is easy. Just call or send us a message. We're ready for you!\n\n### United States\n\n#### Acosta Group\n\n6651 Gate Parkway\n\nJacksonville, FL 32256\n\n### United States\n\n#### Acosta Group\n\n1921 State Highway 121 Ste. #100\n\nLewisville, TX 75056\n\n### United States\n\n#### Premium\n\n618 Spirit Drive\n\nChesterfield, MO 63005\n\n### United States\n\n#### Product Connections\n\n1602 E. Central Ave. Ste. 20\n\nBentonville, AR 72712\n\n### Canada\n\n#### Acosta Group\n\n2700 Matheson Blvd. East, East Tower, Suite 101\n\nMississauga, ON L4W 4V9\n\n### Canada\n\n#### CORE Foodservice\n\n#101 \u2013 250 Schoolhouse St.\nHi, I'm Gina Acosta, Editorial Director and Associate publisher of Progressive Grocer and I'm so excited to be here today and beautiful Jacksonville, FL with Brian Wynn, President and CEO of Acosta Group. So way back in 1927, a few years after a Progressive Grocer was born, Luis Acosta forever changed the way food was marketed when he founded the Acosta company right here in Jacksonville. Since then, Acosta has grown into a global powerhouse solution provider that provides. Brand owners, retailers and food service operators with seamless access to a complete set of modern, best in class agencies and capabilities that helps them grow. As CEO of the company since 2020, Brian has built a team that has established a leading collective of Omni channel retail marketing and food service agencies [...] of Omni channel retail marketing and food service agencies connecting brands with people at every point in the consumer journey. Brian is focused on positioning Acosta Group as the leading driver of sales growth in the modern marketplace, serving over 3500 clients, including over $60 billion revenue brands and 1100 entrepreneurial brands throughout North America and Europe. Under Brian's leadership, Acosta Group is transforming its business by investing significantly in its strategic capabilities, clients, customers and associates. Before Acosta Group, Brian held executive positions for both traditional CPG companies and service centric businesses across a wide range of functions. Brian spent over 20 years in various leadership roles in the Coca-Cola system, culminating as President of [...] 1mo \n\n Report this comment\n\nAbsolutely insightful! The way Acosta Group leverages decades of expertise to bridge the gaps between channels is a masterclass in growth strategy. It\u0080\u0099s exciting to see such a thoughtful approach to connecting retail, foodservice, and online \u0080\u0094 proving that innovation truly thrives where perspectives intersect.\"\n\nLike Reply  1 Reaction\n\nJo Heron \n\nFounder & President - Sisu Solutions Inc. 20+ years of CPG marketing and channel management expertise\n\n 7mo \n\n Report this comment\n\nVery informative! Thank you for speaking to the point of where foodservice meets retail and assisting client partners grow that \u0080\u009cwhite space\u0080\u009d\n\nLike Reply  2 Reactions   3 Reactions\n\n See more comments \n\nTo view or add a comment, sign in\n\n22,126 followers\n\nView Profile   Follow\nJohn Carroll is President of Acosta Group\u2019s Connected Commerce business, enabling clients to bridge the physical and digital shelves by offering one-stop omnichannel services that drive conversion\u2026\n\nTravis King Headshot\n\nTravis King brings decades of industry experience as President of CORE Foodservice, North America\u2019s most progressive foodservice sales agency. He joined The CORE Group at its inception\u2026\n\nDerek Bowen Headshot\n\nDerek Bowen has led Acosta Group\u2019s Brand Advocacy Solutions since 2020 overseeing several agencies, including ActionLink, Mosaic, Premium Retail Services, Product Connections\u2026 [...] ## Our Leadership\n\nMan standing at end of table.\n\n\u201cAs the connection point between brands and consumers, Acosta Group fuels growth for our partners through seamless cross-agency solutions, creating expansive career opportunities for our associates.\u201d\n\nBrian Wynne, President and Chief Executive Officer\n\n## Executive Leadership\n\nBrian Wynne headshot\n\nA seasoned executive with more than 30 years in the packaged goods industry, Brian Wynne joined Acosta Group as President and Chief Executive Officer in 2020\u2026\n\nMark Rahiya joined Acosta Group as Group President of Omnichannel Sales and Services in 2024, bringing over 25 years of experience in consumer goods, notably\u2026 [...] Todd King joined Acosta Group in 2023, and oversees Acosta Group\u2019s strong financial foundation. With more than 30 years of experience leading the financial and administrative operations of fast-growing global businesses\u2026\n\nAs Chief Global Client Officer, Darian Pickett ensures that our core clients receive tailored, growth-driven solutions, working closely across sales and marketing teams to address evolving needs\u2026\n\nLisa Koth Headshot\n\nAs Chief Strategy Officer, Lisa Koth is responsible for advancing Acosta Group\u2019s strategic plan. She partners closely with the company\u2019s business segments to develop strategies\u2026\n\nSharon Hart Headshot\n## Share this article\n\nShare this article\n\nJACKSONVILLE, Fla., Sept. 16, 2024 /PRNewswire/ -- Acosta Group has announced key leadership appointments aimed at strengthening CPG client and retail customer relationships and driving growth. Mark Rahiya joins as Group President, Omnichannel Sales and Services, and Darian Pickett has been named Chief Global Client Officer. Ashley Roehm has been promoted to President of Acosta Sales Agency, while Jami McDermid will continue as President of CROSSMARK. Lisa Koth will now serve as Acosta Group Chief Strategy Officer and EVP, Acosta Europe, expanding her role to include leadership of Acosta Europe. [...] Lisa Koth will now serve as Acosta Group Chief Strategy Officer and EVP, Acosta Europe, expanding her role to include leadership of Acosta Europe following the company's acquisition of the Dee Set Group in the UK. Koth joined the company as a Senior Strategy Director in 2021 and was promoted to SVP, Acosta Group Chief Strategy Officer in 2022. She has led several critical acquisitions over the past two years, including the organization's recent acquisition of CROSSMARK and Product Connections. [...] DARIAN PICKETT NAMED CHIEF GLOBAL CLIENT OFFICER\n\nDarian Pickett, a seasoned industry veteran and accomplished Acosta Group leader, has been appointed Chief Global Client Officer, representing a significant investment in the organization's clients. Since joining Acosta in 1991, Pickett has held leadership roles across every aspect of the company's operations. He is known for navigating market changes successfully while building and maintaining strong client relationships.\nUnder Brian\u2019s leadership, Acosta Group is transforming its business by investing significantly in its strategic capabilities, clients, customers, and associates. Highlights include creating a full-service digital commerce division, expanding its revenue growth management services and advanced analytics, modernizing its in-store services to be more effective and efficient with data-led alerts, insights and artificial intelligence, and entering new categories, including consumer electronics, with market-leading clients and retailers. With a strong focus on creating value for all the company\u2019s stakeholders, Brian and the Acosta Group team have delivered three consecutive years of profitable growth.\nThe enduring strength of our workforce has an indelible influence on the continued success of our service-focused organization. From our entry-level associates through our leadership teams, we are committed to providing programs designed to engage talent of all kinds, support individual health and well-being, develop personal and professional growth, and unlock opportunities. When each associate is at their best, we are at our best for the brands and retail partners who depend on our expertise.\n10 People PEOPLE \u25a1 OUR PEOPLE Acosta Group is a vibrant, growing entity, and growth creates career opportunities. Our associates can discover and build careers they didn't even think were possible. [...] We are also committed to aligning our business objectives with our core values and ethical standards. We embrace our role as responsible corporate citizens and are committed to maintaining the trust and respect of our stakeholders.\nOn behalf of everyone at Acosta Group, I am grateful for your ongoing support and partnership as we strive to exceed expectations in all that we do. We remain steadfast in our commitment to investing in our people, fostering accountability, improving our operations, delivering great results, and positively impacting our communities. Thank you for your trust in Acosta Group.\nAbout Us\n\n### Build Your Career Here\n\nThe best companies are created through the collective talents of individuals. That's why we're obsessed with developing our people, both personally and professionally.\n\n Early Career Opportunities\n\n### Find Your Fit\n\nWhether you desire the versatility of part-time positions or the commitment of full-time roles, we're your gateway to endless opportunities.\n\nSearch Open Positions\n\n## Beware of Recruitment Scams\n\nYour safety is our priority. Acosta Group and our affiliated agencies will never ask for money during the application process. We only contact candidates using official email addresses ending in: @acosta.com, @actionlink.com, @corefoodservice.com, @crossmark.com, @deeset.co.uk, @mosaic.com, @premiumretail.com, or @productconnections.com. [...] ### Product Connections Careers\n\n    Product Connections creates impactful brand experiences through digital and in-person events, including product sampling, shopper marketing, and more.\n\n    View Openings\n\n    Get to Know Product Connections\n\nItem 1 of 8\n\n## Who We Are\n\nAcosta Group is headquartered in Jacksonville, Florida, but we have thousands of employees and a variety of teams generating sales for our clients all over North America and Europe.\n\nSEARCH U.S. ROLES\n\nSEARCH CANADA ROLES\n\nSEARCH GREAT BRITAIN ROLES\n\n\u201cAcosta Group is a vibrant, growing entity, and growth creates career opportunities. Our associates can explore and build careers they didn't even think were possible.\u201d\n\nBrian Wynne, President and CEO\n\nAbout Us\n\n### Build Your Career Here",
