    "raw_content": "Wikipedia\nThe Free Encyclopedia\n\n## Contents\n\n# Alessi Bakery\n\nAlessi Bakery\n\n|  |  |\n --- |\n| Founded | 1912 |\n| Founder | Nicolo Alessi |\n| Area served | Tampa Florida |\n| Products | Pastries, Cakes, Sandwiches, Wraps |\n| Services | Bakery, Deli, Cakes, Catering |\n| Website |  |\n\nAlessi Bakery is a historic bakery and restaurant in Tampa, Florida. It was founded in 1912 by Nicolo Alessi. The business is incorporated as Phil's Cake Box Bakeries. Take-out, dine-in, and catering are offered, with food including desserts, sandwiches, soups, and breads. The bakery also sells wholesale and opened a $20 million 100,000-square-foot bakery plant off Waters Avenue in Town \u2019N Country, Florida in 2008.\n\nIn 2012 the bakery filed for bankruptcy. It remains open.[citation needed] [...] In May 2018, the long-time[when?] owner of Alessi Bakery, Phil Alessi, died. He had inherited the business from his father, John Alessi, and was responsible for the company's expansion, opening a 100,000 sq.ft. facility in Northwest Tampa, in order to sell their products nationally.\n\n## See also\n\n## References\n\n27\u00b057\u20328.62\u2033N 82\u00b029\u203223.3\u2033W\ufeff / \ufeff27.9523944\u00b0N 82.489806\u00b0W\ufeff / 27.9523944; -82.489806\n\nWikimedia Foundation\nPowered by MediaWiki\nAlessi Bakery is a true Tampa landmark dating back over a century to 1912, making it one of the few historic restaurant establishments in the area. Situated at 2909 W. Cypress Street Alessi, Bakery was first opened on Cherry Street by Nicolo Alessi. He arrived in Tampa from Italy over a hundred years ago, bringing his knowledge of baking and proud European heritage with him. Nicolo Alessi used to deliver the freshest Italian and Cuban bread on horse and wagon to his customers. Nicolo\u2019s son John Alessi, continued his father\u2019s tradition of baking, and he received numerous awards for his cake decorating. Those very same cake recipes have been perfected over the years and these cakes are well-known all over the Tampa Bay area for their personalized touch for weddings or any milestone event. [...] It has been over 100 years since Alessi Bakery\u2019s first inception in 1912. Nicolo\u2019s insistence on quality, hard-work, consistency and customer service inherited by 4 generations has been their perfect recipe for success. Their love, experience, and knowledge have made the Alessi family bakery the most successful and well-known bakery in Tampa offering the finest baked goods, wedding cakes and catering in the Tampa Bay area.\n\n### The Staff\n\n### Melissa Maggiore\n\nCake Designer\n\nFor almost a quarter of a  century now, Melissa Maggiore has been making immaculate confections around Central and Southern Florida. In 2000 she came to Alessi Bakery in Tampa; here her culinary creations have been the star for tens of thousands of nuptials. [...] John\u2019s son Phil, was influenced by his father\u2019s love for the business. He loved helping and working around the bakery with his father. As Phil got older, his dream was to expand Alessi Bakery beyond Tampa Bay. He knew the products were not just good enough to sell locally, but good enough to supply wholesale products to companies nationally, and that they did! Later, a 100,000 square foot manufacturing facility was developed in Northwest Tampa, creating the same high quality baked goods and specialty items patrons have always loved.\nWikipedia\nThe Free Encyclopedia\n\n## Contents\n\n# Alessi Bakery\n\nAlessi Bakery\n\n|  |  |\n --- |\n| Founded | 1912 |\n| Founder | Nicolo Alessi |\n| Area served | Tampa Florida |\n| Products | Pastries, Cakes, Sandwiches, Wraps |\n| Services | Bakery, Deli, Cakes, Catering |\n| Website |  |\n\nAlessi Bakery is a historic bakery and restaurant in Tampa, Florida. It was founded in 1912 by Nicolo Alessi. The business is incorporated as Phil's Cake Box Bakeries. Take-out, dine-in, and catering are offered, with food including desserts, sandwiches, soups, and breads. The bakery also sells wholesale and opened a $20 million 100,000-square-foot bakery plant off Waters Avenue in Town \u2019N Country, Florida in 2008.\n\nIn 2012 the bakery filed for bankruptcy. It remains open.[citation needed] [...] In May 2018, the long-time[when?] owner of Alessi Bakery, Phil Alessi, died. He had inherited the business from his father, John Alessi, and was responsible for the company's expansion, opening a 100,000 sq.ft. facility in Northwest Tampa, in order to sell their products nationally.\n\n## See also\n\n## References\n\n27\u00b057\u20328.62\u2033N 82\u00b029\u203223.3\u2033W\ufeff / \ufeff27.9523944\u00b0N 82.489806\u00b0W\ufeff / 27.9523944; -82.489806\n\nWikimedia Foundation\nPowered by MediaWiki\n### Achievements\n\n[]( [](\n\n### Our History\n\nThe Alessi Bakeries story began in 1912, when our founder Nicolo Alessi first began to offer his European style bread and baked goods to the people of Tampa. Nicolo\u2019s focus on quality helped Alessi Bakeries grow from its humble origins to one of the most respected bakeries in the country. We are proud of our rich history and invite you to learn more about what makes Alessi Bakeries so special.\n\nLearn More\n\nAlessi Bakeries\n\nOur Creations\n\nAlessi BakeryView More\n\nAlessi BakeryView More\n\nAlessi BakeryView More\n\nAlessi BakeryView More\n\nAlessi BakeryView More\n\nAlessi BakeryView More\n\n# SUBSCRIBE FOR SPECIALS\nFor more than a century, Alessi Bakery has been a cornerstone of Tampa Bay. Founded in 1912 by Nicolo Alessi, our bakery has grown through five generations of family leadership, blending European tradition with American innovation.\nIn October 2025, we proudly open our brand-new 20,000 sq. ft. Alessi Bakeries Food Market at 3003 W. Cypress Street\u2014a modern expansion of our heritage and a bold step into the future.\nOur new facility will feature:\nAn expanded bakery with 11 display cabinets of cakes, cookies, and pastries\nA state-of-the-art deli and catering department with multiple live cooking stations\nA caf\u00e9 with healthy breakfast and brunch options, smoothies, acai bowls, and artisan coffee\nWoodfired Neapolitan pizza, rotisserie chicken, gourmet salads, and oven-roasted vegetables [...] A full liquor bar for dining and events\nA family-friendly petting zoo to make every visit memorable\nAt Alessi, our mission remains the same as it was in 1912: to provide quality, consistency, and hospitality with every product we make. With the fifth generation of our family\u2014Philip III and Aidan Alessi\u2014now joining the business, the future of Alessi Bakeries is brighter than ever.\nAlessi Bakeries Food Market \u2013 A Tampa tradition reimagined for the next 100 years. [...] External link for Alessi Bakeries Food Market\n\n## Locations\n\n3003 W Cypress St\n\nTampa, Florida 33609, US\n\n5202 Eagle Trail Drive\n\nTampa, FL 33634, US\n\n## Employees at Alessi Bakeries Food Market\n\nClick here to view Papande Newman\u2019s profile\n\n### Papande Newman\n\nClick here to view jorge alberto mussuto\u2019s profile\n\n### jorge alberto mussuto\n\nClick here to view Frank Turczyn\u2019s profile\n\n### Frank Turczyn\n\nClick here to view Sefik Turan\u2019s profile\n\n### Sefik Turan\n\n## Updates\n\nView organization page for Alessi Bakeries Food Market\n\n1,334 followers\n# Philip Alessi Jr.\nPresident/CEO at Alessi Bakeries\nTampa, Florida, United States, US  \n485 connections, 538 followers\n\n## About\nN/A\n\n## Experience\n### President/CEO  \nAlessi Bakeries  \nJul 2009 - Present   \n5202 Eagle Trail Drive  \n\n### Manager/Promoter  \nAlessi Promotions  \nMay 2011 - May 2014   \nTampa, FL  \n\n### Owner  \nAlessi Woodstone  \nMay 2005 - Jun 2009   \nTampa, FL  \n\n### VP Operations  \nAlessi Bakery  \nJun 1985 - Jun 2004   \n2909 W. Cypress Street  \n\n## Education\nN/A\n\n## Publications\nN/A\n\n## Honors & Awards\nN/A\n\n## Certifications\nN/A\n\n## Volunteering\n- Fundraising for Jr. Diabetes Annual Walk\nJr. Diabetes Association\nChildren\nN/A\n\n## Languages\nN/A\n\n## Organizations\nN/A [...] ## Languages\nN/A\n\n## Organizations\nN/A\n\n## Activity\n- Celebrate every milestone! #LoveWhatMatters Credit: @brucewayne5687 (on Twitter)  \nLiked by Philip Alessi Jr.  \nView Post  \nActivity Image\n\n## People Also Viewed\n- David Beckmann (Bainbridge Home Furnishings) - \n- Tommy DeWitt (SyberStorm, Inc) - \n- Nelson Gill (ACC Performance Products Plus) - \n- Dean Marchese (VIRTUE MEDIA VISIONS NETWORK, LLC) - \n- Jason Cooner (Parisii) - \n- Wendy Kallergis (Greater Miami and the Beaches Hotel Association) - \n- Bill Lumpkin (Insurance Marketing Strategies) - \n- Jeff Bombich (JBSA Career Development) - \n- Daniel Caravette (Sin City Cannabis) - \n- Wanda Farnham (IAB Health Productions, LLC) -\nAlessi Bakery is a true Tampa landmark dating back over a century to 1912, making it one of the few historic restaurant establishments in the area. Situated at 2909 W. Cypress Street Alessi, Bakery was first opened on Cherry Street by Nicolo Alessi. He arrived in Tampa from Italy over a hundred years ago, bringing his knowledge of baking and proud European heritage with him. Nicolo Alessi used to deliver the freshest Italian and Cuban bread on horse and wagon to his customers. Nicolo\u2019s son John Alessi, continued his father\u2019s tradition of baking, and he received numerous awards for his cake decorating. Those very same cake recipes have been perfected over the years and these cakes are well-known all over the Tampa Bay area for their personalized touch for weddings or any milestone event. [...] It has been over 100 years since Alessi Bakery\u2019s first inception in 1912. Nicolo\u2019s insistence on quality, hard-work, consistency and customer service inherited by 4 generations has been their perfect recipe for success. Their love, experience, and knowledge have made the Alessi family bakery the most successful and well-known bakery in Tampa offering the finest baked goods, wedding cakes and catering in the Tampa Bay area.\n\n### The Staff\n\n### Melissa Maggiore\n\nCake Designer\n\nFor almost a quarter of a  century now, Melissa Maggiore has been making immaculate confections around Central and Southern Florida. In 2000 she came to Alessi Bakery in Tampa; here her culinary creations have been the star for tens of thousands of nuptials. [...] Phil continued the father-son tradition, and brought his son, Phil Alessi Jr. to work side-by-side with him as the 4th generation Alessi to carry on the family business. In 2011 Phil Jr. began to remodel the bakery at 2909 W. Cypress Street, adding new menu items, a wonderful area for patrons to enjoy their meals, a large window to watch Alessi\u2019s cake decorators create their famous cakes. He created one of Tampa\u2019s most popular catering departments.\n\nAlthough, Alessi Bakery continues to keep up with the trending market, and the days of delivering bread by horse and wagon are long gone, the old traditional bakery feel is ever present on 2909 W. Cypress Street.\nWikipedia\nThe Free Encyclopedia\n\n## Contents\n\n# Alessi Bakery\n\nAlessi Bakery\n\n|  |  |\n --- |\n| Founded | 1912 |\n| Founder | Nicolo Alessi |\n| Area served | Tampa Florida |\n| Products | Pastries, Cakes, Sandwiches, Wraps |\n| Services | Bakery, Deli, Cakes, Catering |\n| Website |  |\n\nAlessi Bakery is a historic bakery and restaurant in Tampa, Florida. It was founded in 1912 by Nicolo Alessi. The business is incorporated as Phil's Cake Box Bakeries. Take-out, dine-in, and catering are offered, with food including desserts, sandwiches, soups, and breads. The bakery also sells wholesale and opened a $20 million 100,000-square-foot bakery plant off Waters Avenue in Town \u2019N Country, Florida in 2008.\n\nIn 2012 the bakery filed for bankruptcy. It remains open.[citation needed]",
